  "executive_briefing": "In 2026, international tax architectures and global trade policies are undergoing significant operational alignment. Enforcement of the OECD Pillar Two 15% global minimum corporate tax framework has transitioned into active operational compliance across over 140 jurisdictions, prompting multinational enterprises to adjust their cross-border tax planning. In parallel, regional governments across Europe and the ASEAN region are fine-tuning statutory corporate income tax rates, withholding taxes, and non-taxable incentive structures to maintain capital attraction within GloBE constraints. Concurrently, indirect tax administration is shifting toward continuous real-time oversight via mandatory electronic invoicing networks, exemplified by Singapore's phased GST InvoiceNow expansion based on Peppol standards. Meanwhile, international supply chains remain under friction from dynamic tariff modifications, HTS updates, and unilateral trade policy realignments.",
